<!--
  Manual EPG overlay — merged into every output by merge_epg.py as the
  highest-priority source, with no time shift. Use it for events no upstream
  feed labels, e.g. a provider stream with no tvg-id and no guide.

  - Give each channel a dotted country suffix (.au, .uk, .us, .ca) so it lands
    in the right per-country file; overlay channels are always in the slim feed.
  - Write times with their real UTC offset (Sydney: +1000 AEST / +1100 AEDT).
  - Programmes are dropped automatically once they end (settings.prune_ended_hours),
    but delete finished events here too so the channel itself disappears.
  - In TiviMate attach it to a stream: long-press the channel -> Edit -> EPG ->
    pick the overlay channel by its display-name.

  Example (Water Polo World Cup, Jul 2026, on Fox Sports 507):

  <channel id="WaterPoloWC.au">
    <display-name>Water Polo World Cup (Fox 507)</display-name>
  </channel>
  <programme start="20260726180000 +1000" stop="20260726194500 +1000" channel="WaterPoloWC.au">
    <title>Water Polo World Cup — Men's Gold Medal Match</title>
    <category>Sport</category>
  </programme>
-->
